        <div id="is-it-healthy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            9. Is Serious Mass Healthy? Sugar, Diabetes and Other Health Caveats
          </h2>

          <p>
            Serious Mass is not unhealthy for a lean, active adult who needs the calories, but it is a poor fit for anyone managing blood sugar. A full serving contains 253 g of carbohydrate, most of it maltodextrin, which has a high glycemic index and raises blood glucose quickly. The label's 30 g of total sugars understates the impact, because maltodextrin is not counted as sugar even though the body digests it rapidly into glucose.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">HEALTH CAVEAT</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Talk to a doctor first if you have diabetes, prediabetes or kidney disease</p>
            <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed m-0">A full serving of Serious Mass delivers about 253 g of fast-digesting carbohydrate, 200 mg of cholesterol and 680 mg of sodium, per the label. People with diabetes, prediabetes, kidney disease, high blood pressure, or who take medication, are pregnant or have a milk or soy allergy should check with a doctor or registered dietitian before using any mass gainer. Unexplained weight loss also needs a medical check, not a gainer.</p>
          </div>

          <p>
            For people with diabetes, our <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-diabetics/">diabetic-friendly protein powder guide</a> is a better starting point. If you need to gain weight with diabetes, a dietitian will usually build calories from protein, fats and slower carbohydrates rather than a maltodextrin shake, and may suggest a lower-sugar gainer such as Pro Gainer at a reduced dose.
          </p>

          <p>
            There are a few other points worth weighing. The cholesterol (200 mg) and saturated fat (3 g) are moderate, and sodium at 680 mg is about 30% of the daily value in a single shake. The sweeteners, sucralose and acesulfame potassium, are approved for use, but some buyers prefer to avoid them, which is the main reason to consider Naked Mass instead. And 5 g of creatine a day is a well-studied dose for healthy adults, though people with kidney disease should get medical advice before taking creatine in any form.
          </p>

          <p>
            Used as intended, as a calorie supplement alongside real meals and hard training, Serious Mass does its job. The risk is using it as a meal replacement or drinking it without training, which tends to add fat rather than muscle. Teenagers who want to gain weight should generally start with more food and a standard protein powder before reaching for a 1,260-calorie gainer.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-should-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Who Should Buy Serious Mass, and Who Should Skip It?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Serious Mass suits true hard gainers: people who are underweight or very lean, have small appetites, train with weights and cannot eat enough to gain. For them, a cheap source of more than 1,000 drinkable calories with 50 g of protein and 5 g of creatine solves a real problem. Athletes in high-volume sports such as rowing, rugby or endurance training, who burn thousands of calories a day, can also use it to close the gap.
          </p>

          <p>
            It does not suit people who want lean muscle with minimal fat gain, anyone with diabetes or prediabetes, anyone sensitive to lactose, or drug-tested athletes who need a certification mark. It also makes little sense for people who simply want more protein, because they are paying for 1,000 carbohydrate calories they do not need. For those readers, a standard whey is cheaper and more flexible; our <a href="/best-protein-powder-with-creatine/">protein powders with creatine</a> list covers options that keep the creatine without the carbohydrate load.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">A simple way to decide</h3>

          <p>
            Ask how many calories you need to add each day. If the answer is more than 1,000 and you have tried eating more food without success, Serious Mass, at a half serving to start, is a reasonable tool. If the answer is 400 to 700, Pro Gainer or a whey shake with milk and oats fits better. If you want the Serious Mass dose without artificial sweeteners, choose Naked Mass and add your own flavor.
          </p>

          <p>
            Whatever you choose, judge it by the scale and the mirror over four to six weeks, not by the first shake. Our full <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-weight-gain/">best protein powder for weight gain</a> roundup compares the gainers and whey proteins we rate most highly, ranked by label and cost per 25 g of protein.
          </p>
        </div>

