            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Starting at the full 340 g serving</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Two heaping scoops in one shake is about 1,260 calories and 253 g of carbohydrate. That is the main cause of the bloating buyers report. ON itself suggests half a serving for the first week. Start there, split doses across the day and increase only if your stomach copes and the scale is not moving.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating it as a protein powder</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Only about 16% of Serious Mass calories come from protein. At roughly $3.30 to $3.62 per 25 g of protein at the prices we saw, it costs about double a regular whey. If you only want more protein, buy a protein powder and keep the gainer for days you need calories.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Doubling up on creatine</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Each full serving already contains 5 g of creatine monohydrate, the standard daily dose. Adding a separate 5 g scoop doubles your intake with no extra benefit for most people. If you take a half serving, you get 2.5 g, so a small top-up is reasonable; otherwise drop the extra creatine.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Shaking instead of blending</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                With 340 g of powder in 24 fl oz of liquid, a shaker bottle tends to leave clumps and a gritty texture. ON's directions call for 30 to 45 seconds in a blender, and buyers who follow them report far smoother shakes. Add the liquid first and the powder second to avoid a dry pocket at the bottom.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the sugar if you have blood sugar issues</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The label lists 30 g of sugars, but the 253 g of maltodextrin behind it digests quickly into glucose. That makes Serious Mass a risky choice for people with diabetes or prediabetes. Speak to a doctor or registered dietitian first, and consider a lower-carbohydrate option such as Pro Gainer.
              </p>
            </div>
